{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateParameterPlanck","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateParameterPlanck","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.hbar_q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.hbar_q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-planck.lean#L28-L44","doc":"When `q ≠ 1`, the quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹` is nonzero.\n\n`hbar_q` is a structure field carrying the default value `1 - q⁻¹`;\nthe hypothesis `hdef` records that the constant takes this canonical\nvalue (it holds for any instance built without overriding the field).\nThis is the definitional content of `\\hbar_q = 1 - q^{-1}` in the\nnarrative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck.hbar_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck.hbar_q","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-planck.lean#L26-L26","doc":"The quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck.hq_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck.hq_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-planck.lean#L24-L24","doc":"`q ≠ 0`, ensuring the Hopf algebra is well-defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck.q","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-planck.lean#L22-L22","doc":"The substrate parameter `q ∈ ℂ`, nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck.mk","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-planck.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateParameterPlanck","kind":"structure","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-planck.lean#L16-L26","doc":"**SubstrateParameterPlanck**: the deformation parameter `q ∈ ℂ*`\nand the derived quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:substrate-parameter-planck}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:substrate-parameter-planck","label":"def:substrate-parameter-planck","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter-planck.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}